      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5dbcd0d4b4180224b42bfbe2",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This can't be done for two reasons.\n\nReason 1: PC avatars are too powerful for Quest. The limits for Quest avatars are way lower than the PC ones, and a single avatar could make you crash.\n\nReason 2: PC VRChat is a desktop game, Quest VRChat is an android game. The quest uses a mobile processor and a OS based on Android. When exporting avatars for Quest from Unity you have to convert the project to Android first, so the format is different as well.\n\nIf you want to play in the PC version with the Quest you need to get a link cable.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
